======================================================================
25. ROLLOUT-WIDE VALID-SAMPLE BC NORMALIZATION
======================================================================

A scientific weighting bug was found in the current AS student objective.
BC was divided independently by each minibatch's valid-mask count.  With
contiguous time-major minibatches, valid density differs across minibatches
because default-pose and initial-step masks are structured in time.  The old
formula consequently gave one sparse minibatch the same aggregate influence
as one dense minibatch and over-weighted each sparse valid sample.

The corrected implementation computes the global weighted number of valid BC
samples once over the filled rollout, divides it by the number of
minibatches, and injects that fixed denominator into every BC loss path:
ordinary hybrid DAgger, supervised-only updates, non-streamed microbatches,
and streamed backward.  A per-minibatch global presence reduction is retained
so an all-empty pure-BC minibatch still skips the optimizer step without
changing collective order.  If `V = sum_r(weight_r * valid_r)`, world size is
`W`, and there are `M` minibatches, each local BC sum is divided by
`(V/W)/M`; DDP's weighted SUM/W then makes the average of the M step gradients
equal the global valid-sample mean.  The same denominator on each epoch and
each streamed microbatch is intentional and mathematically correct.

Uneven-mask gradient-equivalence tests, DDP denominator tests, multi-epoch
reasoning, and streamed collective-order review passed.  The combined PPO,
student, fixed-BC, schedule, storage, module, resume, locomotion and rank-local
suite passed 470 tests (six expected external-xFormers warnings only).

Formal r21 uses its older immutable snapshot and therefore still has the
per-minibatch denominator.  It remains useful as a health and diagnostic run,
but it is no longer a final scientific result and must not be used to decide
the corrected student's objective quality.  A fresh replacement should be
launched from a final new snapshot after validation and when the authorized
GPUs can be safely reassigned; the healthy owned r21 session is not killed
before that boundary.

